<Page
    x:Class="Planillium.App.Pages.SettingsPage"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!--
        A section list on the RIGHT, one section shown at a time, in a content pane whose
        rectangle never changes (2026-08-04, replacing the collapsible Expanders shipped earlier
        the same day at the user's direction: "put an additional sub-menu on the right side, the
        settings pages should be of the same size with no bouncing").

        The no-bouncing property is structural, not cosmetic — three things create it, and all
        three are load-bearing:
          * The outer Grid fills the frame: row 1 takes ALL remaining height (`*`), so the
            content rectangle is a function of the window, never of which section is selected.
            Sections taller than it scroll inside it; shorter ones leave whitespace below.
          * Every section panel lives in the SAME Grid cell with exactly one Visible. Collapsed
            siblings are not measured, so a tall section can't pad a short one — and, more to the
            point, no section can push the status line or the menu around.
          * The status strip is a fixed-height row. Left to size itself it would grow by a line
            the moment a save message appeared and shrink again when it cleared, which is the
            bounce this layout exists to remove.

        Why a menu is safe here even though everything on this page saves as one group: every
        section's controls are loaded and stay loaded whether or not they're on screen, and
        SaveRules writes all of them in one Mutate regardless of what's selected. Hiding a
        section hides the controls, not their values.

        The right side rather than the left is deliberate: the app's own NavigationView pane is
        already on the left, and a second left-hand menu immediately beside it reads as one
        two-level tree, where clicking "Reports" and clicking "Scoring" look like the same kind of
        move. Facing it across the content pane keeps the page-level and within-page navigation
        visibly different things.

        Each menu entry carries a live summary of that section's current values, so the menu
        doubles as an at-a-glance settings overview instead of being seven labels — the property
        the Expander headers had, kept. Summaries are refreshed by RefreshSummaries().

        Widths are set for the app's MINIMUM window (900dip: 248 nav pane + 40 padding + 200 menu
        + 16 gap leaves ~388 for content), not for the comfortable case. Everything below fits in
        388 or reflows to fit it — the scoring grid drops to one column, see LayoutScoringGrid.
        This page has twice shipped controls that were silently clipped at real window sizes
        (2026-07-21, 2026-07-28); narrow is the case worth designing against.
    -->
    <Grid Padding="20,8,20,12" ColumnSpacing="16">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="200"/>
        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

        <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Spacing="4" Margin="0,4,0,12">
            <TextBlock Text="Settings" Style="{StaticResource TitleTextBlockStyle}"/>
            <!-- Above the menu, not inside a section: this is live status, not a setting, and
                 putting it behind a menu entry would mean "is it actually tracking?" costs a
                 click and a guess about which entry holds it. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="TrackerInfo" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- ══ content pane ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
        <ScrollViewer x:Name="SectionScroll" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0"
                      VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollMode="Disabled"
                      Padding="0,0,4,0">
            <!-- The cap lives on a COLUMN, not on the Grid: `MaxWidth` plus
                 `HorizontalAlignment="Left"` would make this Grid size to its content instead of
                 to the space it's given, and every star column inside the sections would then
                 collapse to the width of its own text — the same silent under-sizing the
                 Expanders needed `HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch"` to avoid. A capped star
                 column stretches up to the cap and stops, which is what's wanted: on a wide
                 window the explanatory paragraphs would otherwise run to ~110 characters a line
                 and the controls stretch with them (a 284px box holding "08:00"). Below the cap
                 everything still shrinks to fit, which is what keeps the narrow case working. -->
            <Grid>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*" MaxWidth="820"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <StackPanel x:Name="GeneralPanel" Spacing="16" VerticalAlignment="Top">
                    <TextBlock Text="General" Style="{StaticResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}"/>
                    <!-- Previously set once at first run (NameSetupDialog) with no way to see or
                         change it afterward short of opening config.json directly
                         (2026-07-18 audit finding R10-13). -->
                    <TextBox x:Name="YourName" Header="Your name" Width="260" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                             PlaceholderText="e.g. Alex" LostFocus="YourName_Changed"/>
                    <RadioButtons x:Name="ThemeChoice" Header="Theme" SelectionChanged="Theme_Changed">
                        <RadioButton Content="Follow Windows (recommended)" Tag="default"/>
                        <RadioButton Content="Light" Tag="light"/>
                        <RadioButton Content="Dark" Tag="dark"/>
                    </RadioButtons>
                    <Slider x:Name="OpacitySlider" Header="Window opacity (%)" Width="260"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Left" Minimum="40" Maximum="100"
                            StepFrequency="5" TickFrequency="10" TickPlacement="Outside"
                            ValueChanged="Opacity_Changed"/>
                    <ToggleSwitch x:Name="StartupToggle" Header="Start with Windows (minimized to the tray)"
                                  Toggled="Startup_Toggled"/>
                </StackPanel>

                <StackPanel x:Name="HoursPanel" Spacing="16" VerticalAlignment="Top" Visibility="Collapsed">
                    <TextBlock Text="Hours &amp; reminders" Style="{StaticResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}"/>
                    <!-- Star columns rather than a horizontal StackPanel, here and in the two
                         rows below: a StackPanel hands each child its desired width and lets the
                         overflow fall off the right edge with no error, which is exactly how
                         RetentionDays and LateDayReminderHours came to render as slivers in
                         2026-07-21. Star columns shrink instead, and MinWidth stops the shrink
                         before a NumberBox header (which does not wrap) starts clipping. -->
                    <Grid ColumnSpacing="12">
                        <!-- Capped on the COLUMN rather than the control: a MaxWidth on the TextBox
                             centres it in whatever the column turns out to be, so the left edges of
                             consecutive rows stop lining up. Capping the column packs them left. -->
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*" MaxWidth="150"/><ColumnDefinition Width="*" MaxWidth="150"/><ColumnDefinition Width="*" MaxWidth="150"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <TextBox x:Name="WorkStart" Grid.Column="0" Header="Work start" MinWidth="100" PlaceholderText="08:00" LostFocus="Rules_Changed"/>
                        <TextBox x:Name="WorkEnd" Grid.Column="1" Header="Work end" MinWidth="100" PlaceholderText="20:00" LostFocus="Rules_Changed"/>
                        <TextBox x:Name="EodTimeBox" Grid.Column="2" Header="Day review at" MinWidth="100" PlaceholderText="20:00" LostFocus="Rules_Changed"/>
                    </Grid>
                    <!-- No separate diary-window pair here on purpose (2026-08-04): the diary logs
                         exactly the working hours above. Two pairs of hours was one pair too many. -->
                    <TextBlock Text="Your activity is recorded only between these hours. Outside them nothing is tracked, and time away isn't counted against you."
                               TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12" Margin="2,-8,0,0"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                    <Grid ColumnSpacing="12" RowSpacing="16">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*" MaxWidth="240"/><ColumnDefinition Width="*" MaxWidth="240"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/><RowDefinition Height="Auto"/><RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <NumberBox x:Name="GraceMin" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Header="Grace before alert (min)" MinWidth="170" Minimum="1" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Compact" ValueChanged="Rules_ValueChanged"/>
                        <NumberBox x:Name="RepeatMin" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Header="Repeat every (min)" MinWidth="150" Minimum="1" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Compact" ValueChanged="Rules_ValueChanged"/>
                        <NumberBox x:Name="IdleMin" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Header="Idle after (min)" MinWidth="130" Minimum="1" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Compact" ValueChanged="Rules_ValueChanged"/>
                        <!-- Maximum added (2026-07-18 audit finding R11-10): unbounded, this could
                             silently defeat the app's own documented "kept for a configurable
                             number of days, 90 by default" retention promise. -->
                        <NumberBox x:Name="RetentionDays" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Header="Keep detailed diary (days)" MinWidth="170" Minimum="1" Maximum="3650" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Compact" ValueChanged="Rules_ValueChanged"/>
                        <!-- Header shortened from "Warn if tasks open, before day ends (hrs)"
                             (2026-08-04): at this column width the old one clipped, and a clipped
                             NumberBox header is silent — it just reads as a different setting. -->
                        <NumberBox x:Name="LateDayReminderHours" Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Header="Warn before day ends (hrs)" MinWidth="170" Minimum="0.25" Maximum="12" SmallChange="0.25" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Compact" ValueChanged="Rules_ValueChanged"/>
                    </Grid>
                    <TextBlock Text="The warning fires that many hours before your day review, if tasks are still open."
                               TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                </StackPanel>

                <StackPanel x:Name="ScoringPanel" Spacing="12" VerticalAlignment="Top" Visibility="Collapsed">
                    <TextBlock Text="Scoring" Style="{StaticResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}"/>
                    <!-- Populated in code from ScoringRules.All rather than hand-listed here: the table
                         already holds every key, default and range, and a second hand-typed copy in XAML
                         is precisely the drift this project keeps getting bitten by. Column count is
                         chosen from the measured width (LayoutScoringGrid) because these labels are the
                         longest on the page and a NumberBox header neither wraps nor complains. -->
                    <Grid x:Name="ScoringGrid" ColumnSpacing="12" RowSpacing="12" SizeChanged="ScoringGrid_SizeChanged"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="Changing these affects days scored from now on. Days already closed keep the score they were credited with — they're only recalculated if you edit that day's diary."
                               TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                </StackPanel>

                <StackPanel x:Name="KeywordsPanel" Spacing="12" VerticalAlignment="Top" Visibility="Collapsed">
                    <TextBlock Text="Activity keywords" Style="{StaticResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="One per line, matched inside window titles. A window whose title contains one of these words is counted as that kind of time."
                               TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               FontSize="12" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                    <Grid ColumnSpacing="12">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/><ColumnDefinition Width="*"/><ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <TextBox x:Name="RulesOn" Grid.Column="0" Header="On-plan" AcceptsReturn="True" Height="220" TextWrapping="NoWrap" LostFocus="Rules_Changed"/>
                        <TextBox x:Name="RulesOff" Grid.Column="1" Header="Off-plan" AcceptsReturn="True" Height="220" TextWrapping="NoWrap" LostFocus="Rules_Changed"/>
                        <TextBox x:Name="RulesNeutral" Grid.Column="2" Header="Neutral" AcceptsReturn="True" Height="220" TextWrapping="NoWrap" LostFocus="Rules_Changed"/>
                    </Grid>
                </StackPanel>

                <StackPanel x:Name="IdlePanel" Spacing="12" VerticalAlignment="Top" Visibility="Collapsed">
                    <TextBlock Text="Idle-answer library" Style="{StaticResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="When you come back from being away and say what you were doing, these words decide how that time is counted. One per line."
                               TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               FontSize="12" Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                    <Grid ColumnSpacing="12">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/><ColumnDefinition Width="*"/><ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <!-- Headers shortened from "Counts as on-plan" etc (2026-08-04): three of
                             those don't fit three columns at this page's minimum width, and the
                             sentence above already says what the columns mean. -->
                        <TextBox x:Name="IdleOn" Grid.Column="0" Header="On-plan" AcceptsReturn="True" Height="200" TextWrapping="NoWrap" LostFocus="Rules_Changed"/>
                        <TextBox x:Name="IdleOff" Grid.Column="1" Header="Off-plan" AcceptsReturn="True" Height="200" TextWrapping="NoWrap" LostFocus="Rules_Changed"/>
                        <TextBox x:Name="IdleNeutral" Grid.Column="2" Header="Neutral" AcceptsReturn="True" Height="200" TextWrapping="NoWrap" LostFocus="Rules_Changed"/>
                    </Grid>
                </StackPanel>

                <StackPanel x:Name="TickTickPanel" Spacing="12" VerticalAlignment="Top" Visibility="Collapsed">
                    <TextBlock Text="TickTick" Style="{StaticResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}"/>
                    <TextBlock x:Name="TickTickStatus" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                        <Button x:Name="TickTickConnectBtn" Content="Connect TickTick…"
                                Click="TickTickConnect_Click" HorizontalAlignment="Left"/>
                        <Button x:Name="TickTickDisconnectBtn" Content="Disconnect TickTick…"
                                Click="TickTickDisconnect_Click" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                Visibility="Collapsed"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </StackPanel>

                <StackPanel x:Name="DataPanel" Spacing="12" VerticalAlignment="Top" Visibility="Collapsed">
                    <TextBlock Text="Data" Style="{StaticResource SubtitleTextBlockStyle}"/>
                    <TextBlock x:Name="DataInfo" TextWrapping="Wrap" IsTextSelectionEnabled="True"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                    <!-- Two by two rather than one row of four (2026-08-04): four buttons side by
                         side needed ~690px, which no longer exists once the menu takes its column.
                         A horizontal StackPanel would have dropped "Clear all my data" off the
                         edge in silence — the same failure this page shipped in 2026-07-21. -->
                    <Grid ColumnSpacing="10" RowSpacing="10" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*" MaxWidth="230"/><ColumnDefinition Width="*" MaxWidth="230"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/><RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <Button x:Name="ExportAllBtn" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Content="Export all my data…"
                                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" Click="ExportAll_Click"/>
                        <Button x:Name="ClearHistoryBtn" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Content="Clear activity history…"
                                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" Click="ClearHistory_Click"
                                Style="{StaticResource DangerButtonStyle}"/>
                        <Button x:Name="ClearReflectionsBtn" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Content="Clear my reflections…"
                                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" Click="ClearReflections_Click"
                                Style="{StaticResource DangerButtonStyle}"/>
                        <Button x:Name="ClearAllDataBtn" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Content="Clear all my data…"
                                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" Click="ClearAllData_Click"
                                Style="{StaticResource DangerButtonStyle}"/>
                    </Grid>
                    <TextBlock Text="Export writes every stored row (tasks, notes, score history, activity diary, evening reflections) to one JSON file. Clearing activity history removes the tracked window-activity diary only; clearing reflections removes your evening-review answers only. &quot;Clear all my data&quot; removes everything at once — task completions, reschedules/day-offs, notes, score history, reflections, TickTick sync links, the activity diary, and the debug log — but never your plan definitions themselves (archive or delete those from the Plans page). Your plans, task completions, and score are always untouched by the two narrower buttons above."
                               TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12"
                               Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                </StackPanel>
            </Grid>
        </ScrollViewer>

        <!-- ══ section menu ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
        <Border Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Grid.RowSpan="2" CornerRadius="8"
                Background="{ThemeResource CardBackgroundFillColorDefaultBrush}"
                BorderBrush="{ThemeResource CardStrokeColorDefaultBrush}" BorderThickness="1"
                VerticalAlignment="Top" Padding="4">
            <!-- ListView, not a stack of RadioButtons or hand-toggled Buttons: selection state,
                 arrow-key navigation and the screen-reader "N of 7" announcement all come for
                 free, and the selected-item indicator is the platform's own rather than a colour
                 this page invented.

                 AutomationProperties.Name on every item is not optional: a ListViewItem whose
                 content is a panel rather than a string derives NO accessible name from its
                 children, so a screen reader announced all seven as blank. Caught by reading the
                 UIA tree back (2026-08-04) — nothing about it is visible on screen, which is
                 exactly why it has to be asserted rather than looked at. The name is the
                 destination only; the summary underneath is read as the item's content. -->
            <ListView x:Name="SectionList" SelectionMode="Single" SelectionChanged="Section_Changed">
                <ListViewItem HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch" AutomationProperties.Name="General">
                    <StackPanel Padding="0,4">
                        <TextBlock Text="General" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="13"/>
                        <TextBlock x:Name="SumGeneral" FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxLines="2"
                                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </ListViewItem>
                <ListViewItem HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch" AutomationProperties.Name="Hours and reminders">
                    <StackPanel Padding="0,4">
                        <TextBlock Text="Hours &amp; reminders" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="13"/>
                        <TextBlock x:Name="SumHours" FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxLines="2"
                                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </ListViewItem>
                <ListViewItem HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch" AutomationProperties.Name="Scoring">
                    <StackPanel Padding="0,4">
                        <TextBlock Text="Scoring" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="13"/>
                        <TextBlock x:Name="SumScoring" FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxLines="2"
                                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </ListViewItem>
                <ListViewItem HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch" AutomationProperties.Name="Activity keywords">
                    <StackPanel Padding="0,4">
                        <TextBlock Text="Activity keywords" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="13"/>
                        <TextBlock x:Name="SumKeywords" FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxLines="2"
                                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </ListViewItem>
                <ListViewItem HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch" AutomationProperties.Name="Idle-answer library">
                    <StackPanel Padding="0,4">
                        <TextBlock Text="Idle-answer library" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="13"/>
                        <TextBlock x:Name="SumIdle" FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxLines="2"
                                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </ListViewItem>
                <ListViewItem HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch" AutomationProperties.Name="TickTick">
                    <StackPanel Padding="0,4">
                        <TextBlock Text="TickTick" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="13"/>
                        <TextBlock x:Name="SumTickTick" FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxLines="2"
                                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </ListViewItem>
                <ListViewItem HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch" AutomationProperties.Name="Data">
                    <StackPanel Padding="0,4">
                        <TextBlock Text="Data" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="13"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="Export or clear what's stored" FontSize="11"
                                   TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxLines="2" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorTertiaryBrush}"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </ListViewItem>
            </ListView>
        </Border>

        <!-- ══ status strip ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
        <!-- Fixed height, always present, outside every section: a save is triggered from three
             different sections and its confirmation (or the validation error that blocked it)
             must be visible whichever one you're on. Height is fixed at two lines rather than
             left to the text, so a message appearing or clearing can't resize the content pane
             above it. Longer messages (an export path, say) trim; a tooltip carries the whole
             string, kept in step by the property-changed callback in the constructor, and the
             text stays selectable so a trimmed path can still be copied. -->
        <Border Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Height="40" Margin="0,8,0,0">
            <TextBlock x:Name="SaveStatus" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxLines="2" FontSize="12"
                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       IsTextSelectionEnabled="True"
                       Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
        </Border>
    </Grid>
</Page>
